1
00:00:08,560 --> 00:00:11,080
Turn the lights on and take a look from a distance,
will you?

2
00:00:38,560 --> 00:00:42,640
We'll manage somehow, I'm sure.

3
00:00:44,740 --> 00:00:45,900
You understand, right?

4
00:00:45,900 --> 00:00:47,900
I know, I know.

5
00:00:48,400 --> 00:00:51,760
Once you understand,
keep quiet and follow me.

6
00:01:04,880 --> 00:01:07,080
A final present.

7
00:01:12,760 --> 00:01:14,940
Since I'm at headquarters, right?

8
00:01:16,640 --> 00:01:20,900
Your work is highly regarded
here at headquarters.

9
00:01:21,300 --> 00:01:22,860
Well, when you say my work...

10
00:01:23,260 --> 00:01:27,760
I'm just carrying out the ordinary duties of a police officer,
that's all.

11
00:01:28,160 --> 00:01:30,220
That common sense is what matters most.

12
00:01:30,220 --> 00:01:34,200
Come to headquarters and show
us your skills to the fullest.

13
00:01:34,200 --> 00:01:34,640
Yes.

14
00:01:35,180 --> 00:01:37,840
I will carry out my duties
with utmost sincerity.

15
00:01:38,560 --> 00:01:40,340
Congratulations, Ryotsu-kun.
What a big promotion.

16
00:01:40,520 --> 00:01:42,100
This is all thanks to you, Chief.

17
00:01:42,900 --> 00:01:45,100
It's the fruit of your own efforts.

18
00:01:45,640 --> 00:01:46,000
Well then.

19
00:01:47,900 --> 00:01:50,480
I think the official
announcement will be next month.

20
00:01:50,720 --> 00:01:52,640
Until then, keep this under wraps.

21
00:01:52,860 --> 00:01:53,320
Yes, sir!

22
00:01:56,680 --> 00:01:59,080
Me, transferred to headquarters with honors!

23
00:02:29,980 --> 00:02:32,140
Come on! That Chief!

24
00:02:33,000 --> 00:02:34,940
Is he trying to starve me to death!

25
00:02:35,260 --> 00:02:38,420
He's a demon! A devil! A plague god!

26
00:02:38,560 --> 00:02:41,520
He must have been a wicked
official in his past life!

27
00:02:41,860 --> 00:02:44,860
That's for sure! He looks exactly like one!

28
00:02:44,980 --> 00:02:45,920
S-senpai!

29
00:02:46,060 --> 00:02:46,900
Ryo-chan!

30
00:02:47,140 --> 00:02:49,060
What's wrong with my face!

31
00:02:50,780 --> 00:02:51,900
Ch-Chief!

32
00:02:52,300 --> 00:02:53,660
Good morning, Chief!

33
00:02:53,880 --> 00:02:54,820
Good morning!

34
00:02:55,160 --> 00:02:57,820
Good morning. What were you talking about?

35
00:02:57,820 --> 00:03:02,000
Well, senpai's broke, so he says he
hasn't eaten anything since yesterday.

36
00:03:02,000 --> 00:03:04,220
I bet you went and wasted your
money on some pointless shopping.

37
00:03:04,220 --> 00:03:05,820
Bingo.

38
00:03:05,820 --> 00:03:06,980
That's easy to figure out.

39
00:03:06,980 --> 00:03:10,460
You brought it on yourself. You'll
just have to tough it out until payday.

40
00:03:10,460 --> 00:03:12,880
Do you have any idea how many days are left?

41
00:03:12,880 --> 00:03:19,540
Once I'm transferred to Honmachi A Station,
I won't have to put up with this guy for many more days, will I?

42
00:03:27,260 --> 00:03:28,120
Still,

43
00:03:28,120 --> 00:03:30,540
going without food might affect your work.

44
00:03:30,540 --> 00:03:32,780
Today, I'll treat you to
a meal as a special favor.

45
00:03:32,780 --> 00:03:33,540
Follow me.

46
00:03:35,740 --> 00:03:36,460
What's wrong?

47
00:03:36,460 --> 00:03:37,820
Don't you want to eat?

48
00:03:37,820 --> 00:03:39,900
I'd love to accept your treat!

49
00:03:40,660 --> 00:03:43,040
Chief Ohara treating Ryo-chan?

50
00:03:43,620 --> 00:03:44,620
That's unusual.

51
00:03:52,140 --> 00:03:54,560
Chew well, or it'll be bad for your body.

52
00:03:54,560 --> 00:03:56,380
Did you say something?

53
00:03:57,300 --> 00:03:59,980
Guess you're not the type of
body that breaks down easily

54
00:03:59,980 --> 00:04:02,080
It's nothing. Just eat.

55
00:04:02,580 --> 00:04:04,340
I see. Well then.

56
00:04:09,380 --> 00:04:12,380
How many years has it been
since this place was rebuilt?

57
00:04:12,380 --> 00:04:15,320
I think it's been about
fifteen years already.

58
00:04:15,320 --> 00:04:17,300
Has it really been that long?

59
00:04:17,700 --> 00:04:19,980
I thought it was only recently.

60
00:04:21,660 --> 00:04:23,900
Back when this guy had
just come to the station.

61
00:04:24,500 --> 00:04:27,340
That's when I treated him to a meal like this,
isn't it.

62
00:04:31,600 --> 00:04:34,560
How many years has it been since then?

63
00:04:35,740 --> 00:04:36,140
Thank you very much.

64
00:04:38,600 --> 00:04:41,180
This shopping street
has changed quite a lot.

65
00:04:41,180 --> 00:04:43,360
Has it really changed that much?

66
00:04:43,700 --> 00:04:44,800
It has changed.

67
00:04:44,800 --> 00:04:48,980
Try to remember the time you and
I first went on patrol together.

68
00:04:48,980 --> 00:04:50,840
The change is astonishing.

69
00:04:51,620 --> 00:04:52,340
Is that so?

70
00:04:54,100 --> 00:04:57,500
Well, towns just keep changing, don't they.

71
00:04:59,340 --> 00:05:02,920
You can't possibly remember what it was like long ago,
one by one.

72
00:05:04,340 --> 00:05:05,060
That's enough.

73
00:05:05,060 --> 00:05:06,700
Hey, Chief.

74
00:05:06,700 --> 00:05:09,120
Why are you angry, Chief?

75
00:05:18,180 --> 00:05:20,420
My wife made too much lunch again.

76
00:05:20,420 --> 00:05:23,380
It'd be a waste to throw it out,
so I'll let you have it.

77
00:05:23,380 --> 00:05:25,560
In return, you'd better work hard.

78
00:05:26,540 --> 00:05:27,180
Yes, thank you very much.

79
00:05:29,080 --> 00:05:31,660
Lucky! Now I can eat again today.

80
00:05:31,660 --> 00:05:33,620
Chief's wife is making
lunch at the same time too

81
00:05:33,620 --> 00:05:36,500
Making too much lunch three days in a row?

82
00:05:36,500 --> 00:05:37,880
That's obviously a lie.

83
00:05:39,240 --> 00:05:41,720
He's making it specially for you, senpai.

84
00:05:41,720 --> 00:05:43,580
Otherwise, it wouldn't make sense.

85
00:05:45,040 --> 00:05:48,618
No, this has never happened before.

86
00:05:48,668 --> 00:05:50,120
Maybe he's up to something.

87
00:05:50,260 --> 00:05:51,007
I mean,

88
00:05:51,057 --> 00:05:55,680
Chief Ohara's been acting strange lately, hasn't he?
He's suddenly become so mild-mannered.

89
00:05:55,900 --> 00:05:58,478
Now that you mention it, I can think of a few things.
Senior officer,

90
00:05:58,528 --> 00:06:01,740
hasn't the Chief been yelling at you lately?

91
00:06:02,180 --> 00:06:04,100
Now that you say it, you're right.

92
00:06:04,880 --> 00:06:07,260
Yeah, something like
this happened yesterday.

93
00:06:08,780 --> 00:06:11,740
Terai, did you know this place
used to be a wooden building?

94
00:06:11,740 --> 00:06:15,800
Well, when I got here,
it was already this building.

95
00:06:17,020 --> 00:06:22,260
Is that so? This police box has been around for quite a while,
so I suppose you grow attached to it.

96
00:06:25,900 --> 00:06:29,620
It's almost like they're assigning him to this police box,
sort of.

97
00:06:33,700 --> 00:06:35,820
So the esteemed Ryotsu is finally leaving.

98
00:06:38,180 --> 00:06:42,080
I heard, Chief Ohara,
that you're being promoted to headquarters!

99
00:06:42,080 --> 00:06:45,840
Is that not right?

100
00:06:45,840 --> 00:06:49,040
It's been quite a rumor around
Katsushika Station, though.

101
00:06:53,080 --> 00:06:55,060
I checked with a friend at headquarters.

102
00:06:55,560 --> 00:06:59,140
Chief Ohara's transfer to headquarters
is apparently almost decided.

103
00:07:00,260 --> 00:07:01,960
The official notice is
apparently coming down soon.

104
00:07:02,380 --> 00:07:03,260
So that's how it is.

105
00:07:03,260 --> 00:07:05,480
Chief Ohara is being so distant, too.

106
00:07:05,480 --> 00:07:08,140
He could have just told us, then.

107
00:07:08,140 --> 00:07:10,120
Knowing the Chief's personality,

108
00:07:10,120 --> 00:07:13,480
he probably plans to keep quiet
until the official notice comes down.

109
00:07:13,480 --> 00:07:15,320
Without the Chief around...

110
00:07:16,100 --> 00:07:17,360
It's going to be lonely.

111
00:07:18,180 --> 00:07:19,440
Good riddance!

112
00:07:19,440 --> 00:07:19,980
Ryo-chan.

113
00:07:24,380 --> 00:07:27,700
Hey, shall we all chip in and
get a gift for A store's opening?

114
00:07:27,860 --> 00:07:28,580
Sounds good.

115
00:07:28,580 --> 00:07:29,760
Yeah, let's do it.

116
00:07:30,260 --> 00:07:31,560
I'll chip in too.

117
00:07:32,040 --> 00:07:33,060
What about you, senpai?

118
00:07:33,720 --> 00:07:36,360
Fine, I'll chip in too.

119
00:07:36,360 --> 00:07:38,540
After all, you've looked after me a little.

120
00:07:40,880 --> 00:07:42,380
So what should we give?

121
00:07:43,700 --> 00:07:45,220
A Japanese sword?

122
00:07:46,040 --> 00:07:51,160
According to the chief's wife, he's been
interested in Japanese swords lately.

123
00:07:51,160 --> 00:07:55,500
But there are all sorts
of Japanese swords, right?

124
00:07:55,640 --> 00:07:57,020
And then there's the price, too.

125
00:07:57,020 --> 00:08:02,020
Lately, on his days off, the chief apparently comes
to this department store to look at Japanese swords.

126
00:08:02,020 --> 00:08:04,480
Apparently he has a favorite piece.

127
00:08:05,320 --> 00:08:07,460
Let's give that one for A store's opening.

128
00:08:13,300 --> 00:08:14,640
So they only have wakizashi here?

129
00:08:15,380 --> 00:08:17,240
I guess they'd be a bit longer, right?

130
00:08:17,240 --> 00:08:22,440
Senpai,
it's this short and it's still so expensive!

131
00:08:23,260 --> 00:08:23,660
Alright.

132
00:08:24,160 --> 00:08:24,560
Yes.

133
00:08:24,560 --> 00:08:24,680
Yes.

134
00:08:27,580 --> 00:08:28,280
That one?

135
00:08:30,400 --> 00:08:33,820
Wonderful. No matter how many times I look,
it's a splendid piece.

136
00:08:35,040 --> 00:08:36,020
I'm completely captivated.

137
00:08:37,220 --> 00:08:40,740
That's it! How about we buy it to
commemorate the store's opening?

138
00:08:41,780 --> 00:08:46,140
No, no. As police officers, we shouldn't get
carried away and make impulse purchases like that.

139
00:08:46,720 --> 00:08:48,400
This is just like Ryotsu.

140
00:08:48,400 --> 00:08:53,440
Headquarters appreciated my
qualities as a proper police officer.

141
00:08:54,560 --> 00:08:55,320
I have to be patient.

142
00:09:02,480 --> 00:09:04,960
So this is the one the Chief was looking at.

143
00:09:05,860 --> 00:09:11,740
A million yen?
Senpai, are you really going with this one?

144
00:09:11,740 --> 00:09:19,220
Sure, even as a store opening gift, it's way too expensive.
This is a promotion gift.

145
00:09:19,220 --> 00:09:25,980
You're a senior constable now too, so you'd better dress a little sharper.
Wow, these really are expensive clothes.

146
00:09:26,760 --> 00:09:35,340
What? If you're going to give a promotion gift anyway, something like plastic models would be better.
You idiot, do you have any idea how much this cost?

147
00:09:35,340 --> 00:09:40,300
I bought you the finest bath for your sake,
and now...

148
00:09:40,300 --> 00:09:40,780
Honestly!

149
00:09:45,620 --> 00:09:48,220
No, I think I'll go with
this Japanese sword after all.

150
00:09:48,220 --> 00:09:49,080
Senpai.

151
00:09:49,800 --> 00:09:52,300
If we all chip in, we can manage the money.

152
00:09:52,640 --> 00:09:54,080
It's a congratulatory gift
for the Chief's promotion.

153
00:09:54,520 --> 00:09:56,740
We have to give him the best present.

154
00:09:58,460 --> 00:09:59,540
Delivery for you.

155
00:09:59,540 --> 00:10:00,540
Thank you for your trouble.

156
00:10:03,140 --> 00:10:04,700
It finally arrived

157
00:10:05,160 --> 00:10:07,960
I can't believe we actually bought a
Japanese sword that costs a million yen.

158
00:10:07,960 --> 00:10:13,820
Almost everyone at the police box chipped in.
That's Chief Ohara's good character

159
00:10:15,260 --> 00:10:19,020
It's really heavy.
It makes me kind of excited, somehow.

160
00:10:19,020 --> 00:10:19,480
Mm.

161
00:10:24,400 --> 00:10:26,580
Alright, here we go. Hup!

162
00:10:27,640 --> 00:10:28,000
Me

163
00:10:33,680 --> 00:10:35,300
What a magnificent piece.

164
00:10:35,300 --> 00:10:36,880
I'm sure he'll be delighted.

165
00:10:36,880 --> 00:10:40,200
Let's keep it a secret until
the announcement at the A store.

166
00:10:40,200 --> 00:10:42,460
Morning.

167
00:10:43,500 --> 00:10:44,880
Good morning.

168
00:10:45,520 --> 00:10:46,500
What's going on?

169
00:10:46,500 --> 00:10:48,540
It's nothing, really.

170
00:10:48,540 --> 00:10:51,120
Ryotsu, what were you just holding?

171
00:10:51,920 --> 00:10:52,800
Nothing.

172
00:10:53,560 --> 00:10:56,780
Chief, about yesterday's report,
I need to talk to you...

173
00:10:58,000 --> 00:10:59,040
No, I was first.

174
00:10:59,040 --> 00:11:02,040
Alright, alright, could you take turns?

175
00:11:07,120 --> 00:11:09,100
I see, that makes sense.

176
00:11:09,100 --> 00:11:12,020
I was about to ask the same thing.

177
00:11:12,020 --> 00:11:13,740
Thanks, sorry for the trouble.

178
00:11:14,400 --> 00:11:15,380
So, where's Terai?

179
00:11:15,540 --> 00:11:17,700
M-me too.

180
00:11:18,640 --> 00:11:20,900
Well, whatever.
I'm heading back to the station.

181
00:11:23,880 --> 00:11:26,980
We're not doing anything wrong,
but my heart's pounding.

182
00:11:28,000 --> 00:11:28,300
Really.

183
00:11:28,300 --> 00:11:30,000
I was surprised.

184
00:11:30,740 --> 00:11:32,380
I'm going out on patrol.

185
00:11:32,820 --> 00:11:33,760
I'll come along too.

186
00:11:34,320 --> 00:11:36,080
I'm going shopping.

187
00:11:36,080 --> 00:11:38,280
Ryo-chan,
please watch the place while we're gone.

188
00:11:39,780 --> 00:11:48,560
The Chief suddenly showed up earlier.

189
00:11:48,560 --> 00:11:50,380
We didn't get a good look at it.

190
00:11:51,360 --> 00:11:53,660
The real thing really does have presence

191
00:11:54,300 --> 00:11:55,340
This weight.

192
00:11:55,340 --> 00:11:56,440
This shine.

193
00:11:58,000 --> 00:12:02,100
Makes sense. Back in the day, people
wore these at their waists, after all.

194
00:12:02,530 --> 00:12:07,260
If I'd lived in the Edo period,
I'd surely have become a famous samurai.

195
00:12:12,460 --> 00:12:13,320
Hyaah!

196
00:12:16,820 --> 00:12:23,060
Now that you know my domain's secret, I can't just let you go.
I'm only a bounty hunter.

197
00:12:23,060 --> 00:12:26,000
Aren't you mistaking me for
someone named Ryotsu Fuyōnosuke?

198
00:12:26,480 --> 00:12:28,040
I'll finish you off.

199
00:12:29,560 --> 00:12:33,180
Even a pet dog bares its fangs right away.
What troublesome people you are.

200
00:12:34,700 --> 00:12:35,460
Attack!

201
00:12:47,360 --> 00:12:48,200
Strong.

202
00:12:48,200 --> 00:12:49,620
I'm a clumsy man, you see.

203
00:12:49,980 --> 00:12:52,740
I don't have any fancy
techniques like the mine-uchi.

204
00:12:52,740 --> 00:12:54,880
You'd best come at me with full resolve.

205
00:13:05,120 --> 00:13:08,360
Feel the terror of the Stray Dog Law!

206
00:13:21,040 --> 00:13:23,220
Damn, I chipped a tooth.

207
00:13:25,380 --> 00:13:26,980
This is a bit noticeable, isn't it.

208
00:13:27,580 --> 00:13:30,640
What do we do? It's a present for the Chief.

209
00:13:34,560 --> 00:13:37,360
We have to think of a
way to cover it up somehow.

210
00:13:37,360 --> 00:13:39,820
Hey, where are you going, senpai?

211
00:13:42,340 --> 00:13:43,140
Nakagawa.

212
00:13:43,140 --> 00:13:45,540
That's the Chief's present, isn't it?

213
00:13:45,540 --> 00:13:47,080
Where are you taking it?

214
00:13:47,080 --> 00:13:47,572
Well,

215
00:13:47,622 --> 00:13:51,780
if we leave it at the police box, there's
a risk the Chief will find it, right?

216
00:13:51,780 --> 00:13:54,520
So I thought I'd keep it in my room.

217
00:13:54,520 --> 00:13:56,360
I see, that makes sense.

218
00:13:56,360 --> 00:13:57,140
Right?

219
00:13:57,140 --> 00:13:58,920
But be careful, okay?

220
00:13:58,920 --> 00:14:02,560
If you scratch it,
the present will be ruined.

221
00:14:04,260 --> 00:14:06,480
I know, I know. See you.

222
00:14:08,120 --> 00:14:09,380
If we were to

223
00:14:09,380 --> 00:14:10,640
Just hypothetically, mind you.

224
00:14:10,640 --> 00:14:13,600
if we had this blade polished,

225
00:14:13,600 --> 00:14:15,100
how much would it cost, I wonder?

226
00:14:17,080 --> 00:14:19,700
Depending on the sword's grade,
it's at least around 100,000.

227
00:14:19,700 --> 00:14:22,900
For that sword,
it might cost around 300,000.

228
00:14:22,900 --> 00:14:24,780
300,000

229
00:14:26,060 --> 00:14:27,500
I see, I see.

230
00:14:29,720 --> 00:14:30,380
You've got to be kidding.

231
00:14:30,380 --> 00:14:33,360
We even borrowed money just
to chip in for the gift.

232
00:14:33,740 --> 00:14:35,980
There's no way we can come up with 300,000.

233
00:14:35,980 --> 00:14:37,620
We have no choice but to do it ourselves.

234
00:14:39,700 --> 00:14:41,600
It's still dented about 5 millimeters.

235
00:14:41,600 --> 00:14:45,200
Filing down 5 millimeters across
the whole blade would take forever.

236
00:14:47,480 --> 00:14:50,560
It's rough work, but let's just
grind it down quickly with a grinder.

237
00:14:54,960 --> 00:14:55,280
Right.

238
00:15:01,520 --> 00:15:04,080
The dent's gone,
but now the whole thing's warped.

239
00:15:05,760 --> 00:15:07,560
We'll have to grind it down more.

240
00:15:09,760 --> 00:15:13,020
It's getting even,
but it's turning into a skinnier sword.

241
00:15:13,020 --> 00:15:15,880
It's starting to look like a fencing sword

242
00:15:19,840 --> 00:15:22,260
Oh no, we have to fix it quickly!

243
00:15:25,100 --> 00:15:26,860
So it fits snugly.

244
00:15:26,860 --> 00:15:29,320
It's bent. Start over.

245
00:15:29,320 --> 00:15:33,080
No good, it's already stuck together.

246
00:15:33,960 --> 00:15:35,780
Forget it, who cares about that.

247
00:15:36,340 --> 00:15:38,820
For a gift, a plastic sword is plenty.

248
00:15:38,820 --> 00:15:40,360
There's no need to give a real one.

249
00:15:45,820 --> 00:15:48,340
But it's the Chief's transfer celebration,
after all.

250
00:15:49,220 --> 00:15:53,540
It might be the last present I ever give him,
you know.

251
00:15:54,040 --> 00:15:55,840
But we don't have the money, either.

252
00:15:58,060 --> 00:16:00,200
Senpai isn't here?

253
00:16:00,760 --> 00:16:02,820
He called to say he'd be
taking a break for a while.

254
00:16:02,820 --> 00:16:04,300
Apparently he caught a cold.

255
00:16:04,800 --> 00:16:07,020
On the day the Chief's
transfer is announced,

256
00:16:07,020 --> 00:16:08,780
he's apparently coming in no matter what.

257
00:16:10,360 --> 00:16:11,620
He wants to give the present, apparently.

258
00:16:12,060 --> 00:16:12,920
I see.

259
00:16:14,140 --> 00:16:17,240
But I saw him yesterday, and he seemed fine.

260
00:16:19,960 --> 00:16:21,740
Senpai, are you all right?

261
00:16:22,280 --> 00:16:24,380
I bought some food that
should be nutritious.

262
00:16:25,220 --> 00:16:26,020
Is he sleeping?

263
00:16:26,760 --> 00:16:27,560
Senpai.

264
00:16:27,560 --> 00:16:29,780
Never mind.

265
00:16:32,660 --> 00:16:34,620
What on earth are they doing?

266
00:16:36,500 --> 00:16:36,900
This is...

267
00:16:36,900 --> 00:16:38,880
You saw that, didn't you?

268
00:16:41,360 --> 00:16:43,620
You broke it?! Eeeeeeh!

269
00:16:44,160 --> 00:16:49,240
You broke the gift for Chief Ohara!
Keep your voice down!

270
00:16:49,240 --> 00:16:54,640
Everyone chipped in money! What are we going to do?
We have no choice, so we'll make one ourselves.

271
00:16:54,640 --> 00:17:01,640
Make one ourselves? We got a Japanese blade and tools,
and even borrowed books from the library. Is that okay?

272
00:17:02,360 --> 00:17:08,800
Doable. I made a test one yesterday. Next, we just need to
make something that fits snugly into the original scabbard.

273
00:17:09,280 --> 00:17:12,620
Now that you know about this,
you're going to help us too.

274
00:17:13,060 --> 00:17:15,100
I figured it would come to this.

275
00:17:19,240 --> 00:17:19,960
Let's go.

276
00:17:19,960 --> 00:17:21,180
Okay.

277
00:17:21,180 --> 00:17:21,940
Here.

278
00:17:22,640 --> 00:17:23,240
Yeah, right.

279
00:17:23,240 --> 00:17:27,480
Come on, pull yourself together.

280
00:17:29,800 --> 00:17:30,300
Done!

281
00:17:35,340 --> 00:17:36,120
It's done.

282
00:17:36,120 --> 00:17:38,700
We did it, senpai.

283
00:17:43,600 --> 00:17:45,580
And the size is a perfect fit.

284
00:17:47,500 --> 00:17:49,140
Now I can finally relax.

285
00:17:49,860 --> 00:17:51,960
What's wrong, senpai?

286
00:17:51,960 --> 00:17:55,880
Doesn't this sword look
duller than the last one?

287
00:17:55,880 --> 00:17:56,860
Is that so?

288
00:17:56,860 --> 00:18:04,280
Or... looking closely, the color's a little different too.
I can't really tell, but no, this is no good. It's a failure.

289
00:18:05,220 --> 00:18:12,720
Hey, senpai! This is the Chief's last present.
Do you think I'd send him something half-hearted?

290
00:18:13,260 --> 00:18:16,400
I made it, senpai, so there.

291
00:18:21,240 --> 00:18:21,840
Alright!

292
00:18:57,760 --> 00:18:59,400
Is Ryotsu off sick again today?

293
00:18:59,400 --> 00:19:01,980
Yes, it seems his cold has dragged on.

294
00:19:01,980 --> 00:19:05,720
He said he'd come in tomorrow
even if he has to push himself.

295
00:19:06,080 --> 00:19:07,620
Because tomorrow is the Chief's...

296
00:19:11,380 --> 00:19:14,620
I thought I'd like to spend at
least the last day here with him.

297
00:19:16,080 --> 00:19:18,620
Tomorrow, we have an important
announcement for everyone.

298
00:19:18,620 --> 00:19:20,220
Please come by the station.

299
00:19:20,940 --> 00:19:21,300
Yes.

300
00:19:24,160 --> 00:19:25,500
So it's finally happening.

301
00:19:27,480 --> 00:19:28,740
He's really going to be gone, isn't he.

302
00:19:29,280 --> 00:19:30,460
It's going to be lonely.

303
00:19:44,380 --> 00:19:45,580
It's done!

304
00:19:48,600 --> 00:19:52,920
This is it! This color!
This shine! It's the real deal!

305
00:19:53,440 --> 00:19:57,760
I ended up making over
twenty before I got this one.

306
00:19:58,220 --> 00:20:00,580
I hate to say it myself,
but it turned out great.

307
00:20:00,580 --> 00:20:03,060
With this, no one will think it's a fake.

308
00:20:03,640 --> 00:20:05,800
Oh no, it's already this late!
Wake up, Honda!

309
00:20:05,800 --> 00:20:06,760
Oh no.

310
00:20:08,980 --> 00:20:10,920
Full speed ahead, fisherman, sir!

311
00:20:10,920 --> 00:20:12,480
Will we make it in time?

312
00:20:15,080 --> 00:20:17,140
Today I have some happy news.

313
00:20:17,140 --> 00:20:21,720
Chief Ohara is being
transferred to the Honjo branch.

314
00:20:22,920 --> 00:20:24,120
Ryo-chan's late, isn't he?

315
00:20:24,520 --> 00:20:26,140
He's still not well, you know.

316
00:20:26,340 --> 00:20:29,820
Maybe we should have gone to pick up the present,
at least.

317
00:20:30,080 --> 00:20:32,460
Chief Ohara, say a few words.

318
00:20:32,700 --> 00:20:33,120
Yes, sir!

319
00:20:36,360 --> 00:20:39,348
As the Chief just mentioned,

320
00:20:39,398 --> 00:20:42,740
I've been transferred to headquarters.

321
00:20:43,000 --> 00:20:45,620
I owe all of this to all of you,
and I'm truly grateful.

322
00:20:45,880 --> 00:20:47,620
It's me who should be thanking you!

323
00:20:48,740 --> 00:20:49,380
Fumi-chan!

324
00:20:50,400 --> 00:20:51,060
Ryo...tsu.

325
00:20:52,920 --> 00:20:53,580
Ryo-san.

326
00:20:53,580 --> 00:20:54,220
Thank goodness.

327
00:20:54,220 --> 00:20:54,980
We made it in time.

328
00:20:58,460 --> 00:21:00,960
Thank you for all your help until now.

329
00:21:00,960 --> 00:21:02,100
Ryotsu.

330
00:21:03,300 --> 00:21:06,040
This is a token of thanks
from everyone at the box.

331
00:21:06,040 --> 00:21:07,480
F-for me?

332
00:21:10,240 --> 00:21:12,740
We all chipped in and bought it.

333
00:21:13,280 --> 00:21:15,980
It's the Japanese sword
you were wanting, Chief.

334
00:21:15,980 --> 00:21:17,620
You lot...

335
00:21:17,620 --> 00:21:20,020
Ohara-kun, take it out and let me see.

336
00:21:26,800 --> 00:21:27,980
Aaaaah!

337
00:21:29,460 --> 00:21:35,380
We can't accept something like this!
What do we do if it gets found out, boss?

338
00:21:36,480 --> 00:21:37,880
What's wrong with it, I wonder?

339
00:21:38,620 --> 00:21:41,820
Don't you like it? Like it? Of course we do!

340
00:21:41,820 --> 00:21:43,960
I'm so sorry, I'm ashamed.

341
00:21:43,960 --> 00:21:44,860
Ryotsu!

342
00:21:44,860 --> 00:21:47,960
That's a fake I made myself.

343
00:21:48,740 --> 00:21:49,700
Actually...

344
00:21:49,700 --> 00:21:53,320
I broke the original sword,
so I made this one myself.

345
00:21:54,300 --> 00:21:55,760
Is that true, Ryotsu?

346
00:21:56,260 --> 00:21:57,640
I'm sorry.

347
00:21:58,200 --> 00:21:59,280
What are we going to do now?

348
00:21:59,280 --> 00:22:01,020
Let's tell the truth.

349
00:22:01,760 --> 00:22:03,740
You made this?

350
00:22:06,100 --> 00:22:07,360
Splendid.

351
00:22:07,360 --> 00:22:11,100
I've never seen such a
magnificent Japanese sword.

352
00:22:11,100 --> 00:22:14,120
If it were appraised, it probably
wouldn't go for less than ten million yen.

353
00:22:14,760 --> 00:22:16,480
The reason I said I
couldn't accept it earlier

354
00:22:16,480 --> 00:22:19,140
is that I thought it was
far too valuable an item.

355
00:22:20,700 --> 00:22:22,660
You actually made a sword that good?

356
00:22:23,040 --> 00:22:26,980
You made one even better than the one you bought,
just so no one would find out.

357
00:22:26,980 --> 00:22:28,520
That's not all.

358
00:22:29,060 --> 00:22:32,540
We just wanted to give the Chief
something even a little better.

359
00:22:33,420 --> 00:22:36,600
To the very end,
you always managed to surprise me.

360
00:22:36,600 --> 00:22:42,140
Chief, as a final keepsake, show us
your famous kendo forms with that sword.

361
00:22:43,900 --> 00:22:44,620
Alright.

362
00:22:52,540 --> 00:22:55,340
Hah!

363
00:22:55,340 --> 00:22:57,340
Hah!

364
00:22:58,980 --> 00:23:01,120
Nice.

365
00:23:01,120 --> 00:23:04,540
Bravo!

366
00:23:11,300 --> 00:23:12,760
Crude, I'm afraid.

367
00:23:29,580 --> 00:23:31,380
Ohara-kun,

368
00:23:31,380 --> 00:23:33,180
from headquarters,

369
00:23:34,540 --> 00:23:37,840
it's about your transfer, Ohara-kun.
I brought you the transfer order, but

370
00:23:39,780 --> 00:23:41,380
it seems you won't be needing it.

371
00:23:41,380 --> 00:23:44,180
Let's pretend this whole
business never happened.

372
00:23:44,180 --> 00:23:45,060
Uuugh...

373
00:23:45,060 --> 00:23:46,840
Ah, wait, hold on!

374
00:23:47,360 --> 00:23:48,720
Uuugh...

375
00:23:48,720 --> 00:23:50,040
Chief,

376
00:23:50,040 --> 00:23:52,760
you really are my jinx!

377
00:23:52,760 --> 00:23:54,440
Chief, that's dangerous!

378
00:23:54,440 --> 00:23:56,400
If you keep swinging that sword around,

379
00:23:56,400 --> 00:23:57,940
it's dangerous!

380
00:23:57,940 --> 00:24:00,020
It's not my fault.

381
00:24:00,880 --> 00:24:01,980
Yeah, just as I thought.

382
00:24:01,980 --> 00:24:02,860
Sigh.

383
00:24:05,720 --> 00:24:07,180
I wonder why.

384
00:24:15,440 --> 00:24:19,440
Lemon-chan is a kindergartener, yet

385
00:24:19,440 --> 00:24:22,620
she loves period dramas. I wonder why.

386
00:24:23,880 --> 00:24:28,720
the Chief's little mustache is somehow tiny.
I wonder why.

387
00:24:28,720 --> 00:24:30,380
I wonder why.

388
00:24:30,380 --> 00:24:35,460
Honda-san's personality changes
when he rides his motorcycle.

389
00:24:35,460 --> 00:24:36,580
I wonder why.

390
00:24:36,580 --> 00:24:38,320
I wonder why.

391
00:24:38,320 --> 00:24:42,300
Higurashi Neruo only wakes
up once every four years.

392
00:24:42,300 --> 00:24:43,460
I wonder why.

393
00:24:43,460 --> 00:24:45,560
I wonder why.

394
00:24:46,340 --> 00:24:52,600
Nakagawa won't lend money to Ryotsu,

395
00:24:52,600 --> 00:24:56,340
but he lends out tanks and
fighter planes with ease.

396
00:24:56,340 --> 00:25:00,220
I wonder why.

397
00:25:01,840 --> 00:25:06,980
Reiko is incredibly rich, yet

398
00:25:08,860 --> 00:25:12,500
she works at the police box. I wonder why.

399
00:25:13,320 --> 00:25:14,840
I wonder why.

400
00:25:14,840 --> 00:25:16,000
I wonder why.

401
00:25:16,640 --> 00:25:19,560
Why, why, why, why, I wonder why.

402
00:25:30,580 --> 00:25:33,920
Whoa, what's going on?
I've turned into Reiko!

403
00:25:33,920 --> 00:25:36,980
Ugh, why have I turned into Ryo-chan?

404
00:25:36,980 --> 00:25:39,520
Damn it, this must be another one
of that mad professor's schemes.

405
00:25:39,520 --> 00:25:41,880
Please, change me back quickly!

406
00:25:42,380 --> 00:25:44,420
Next time, I'm Reiko...

407
00:25:44,420 --> 00:25:45,620
And I'm Ryo-chan.

408
00:25:46,060 --> 00:25:46,860
Nice to meet you.

409
00:25:48,660 --> 00:25:50,720
Over there, it's Kameari.

410
00:25:52,020 --> 00:25:54,040
I'm sure it's Kameari.

411
00:25:55,380 --> 00:25:59,220
Everyone, come on over to our town!

412
00:26:00,140 --> 00:26:00,800
Thank you.

